I run NH3.1 it accesses the hard disc every time you do something. G*d, when
you _run_, you can go and eat something, then go back and see if your char
has finished running!

Last weekend I had the chance to try this game on a 386 with 4M emm memory
(optionally qmm). The other memory did not speed up the game, while the other
did. Only, every no and then it would say
	Suddenly, the dungeon collapses.
	Cannot get {n} bytes. (where n is a two to four digit number)
Great. It was still unplayable, not for its slowness, but because 99% of your
games ended in panic. No game could go on for more than 1000 moves or so...

